10.0 Consistency Addendum (Security and Data Integrity)
10.1 URL-to-Payload Subject Binding
For every write endpoint that carries a patient identifier in the URL and patient reference in body payload, the service must enforce strict equality checks before persistence.
Validation sequence: (a) parse URL PatientID, (b) parse body subject.reference, (c) normalize both identifiers, (d) reject request with HTTP 422 if mismatch.

10.2 Encounter Sync Guardrails
The /Encounter/{EncounterID}/_sync endpoint is asynchronous and must require Encounter ownership validation before enqueueing.
If ownership cannot be resolved in <150 ms, enqueue must be denied with 403 rather than accepted optimistically.

10.3 Resolver Boundary Rule
Graph traversal resolvers must re-evaluate authorization at each relationship edge. System service accounts must not bypass caller policy context for reverse-edge traversals.



